% Added from US Customs' publications on fibers and yarns and on household
% articles of plastics, and from rulings (2026-11-21). "vinyl" names a
% plastic but not one polymer (polyvinyl chloride or another vinyl
% polymer): it says only that the good is of plastics. "bamboo" is read as
% the artificial cellulosic fibre made from bamboo, as the publication
% speaks of it. "pu" and "eva" were seller's words of trade usage before a
% ruling stated them.
"polypropylene" is a word for the textile material polypropylene,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "The Explanatory Notes to chapter 54 provides a list of the most common synthetic fibers which include acrylic, modacrylic, polypropylene, nylon and other polyamides".
"viscose rayon" is a word for the textile material viscose,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "Artificial cellulosic fibers include viscose rayon, cuprammonium rayon, and cellulose acetate including tri-acetate.".
"cuprammonium rayon" is a word for the textile material cupro,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "Artificial cellulosic fibers include viscose rayon, cuprammonium rayon, and cellulose acetate including tri-acetate.".
"bamboo" is a word for the textile material viscose,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "Bamboo has recently proved to be an important source for cellulosic artificial fibers.".
"bamboo fiber" is a word for the textile material viscose,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "Bamboo has recently proved to be an important source for cellulosic artificial fibers.".
"bamboo fibre" is a word for the textile material viscose,
    as stated in the fibers and yarns publication, confer "Bamboo has recently proved to be an important source for cellulosic artificial fibers.".
"pu" is a word for the polymer polyurethane,
    as stated in ruling NY N336251, confer "The belt is constructed from 100% polyurethane (PU) plastic material.".
"eva" is a word for the polymer ethylene-vinyl acetate copolymer,
    as stated in ruling NY N296512, confer "ethylene vinyl acetate (EVA) plastic".
"hdpe" is a word for the polymer polyethylene,
    as stated in ruling NY N286927, confer "raw flakes of high-density polyethylene (HDPE)".
"ldpe" is a word for the polymer polyethylene,
    as stated in ruling NY N360188, confer "and low-density polyethylene (LDPE)".
"vinyl" is a word for plastics,
    as stated in the household articles publication, confer "the type of plastic (e.g., vinyl generally being more substantial than polyethylene)".

rule textile_by_construction with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "does not apply to materials regarded as textile materials of Section XI":
a good is a textile article
    if the fabric construction of the good is a construction.

rule textile_by_cut with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "does not apply to materials regarded as textile materials of Section XI":
a good is a textile article
    if the cut of the good indicates a gender.

rule polymer_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
the polymer of a good is a polymer
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for the polymer the polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

rule plastics_by_polymer with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a good is made of plastics
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for the polymer a polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

rule plastics_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "the expression \"plastics\" means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a good is made of plastics
    if the good names the material a name
    and the name is a word for plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a textile article.

scenario case is:
    case names the material "pvc".
    shirt names the material "acrylic".
    the cut of shirt indicates women.
    the fabric construction of scarf is woven.
    scarf names the material "nylon".
    bead names the material "acrylic".
    lens names the material "pmma".
    polymers expects answers ["the polymer of case is polyvinyl chloride", "the polymer of bead is acrylic polymer", "the polymer of lens is polymethyl methacrylate"].
    plastics expects answers ["case is made of plastics", "bead is made of plastics", "lens is made of plastics"].
    fibres expects answers ["lycra is a word for the textile material elastane"].
    goat fibres expects answers ["mohair is a word for the textile material mohair"].

scenario rulings is:
    belt names the material "pu".
    glove names the material "vinyl".
    the cut of tee indicates men.
    tee names the material "polypropylene".
    ruling_polymers expects answers ["the polymer of belt is polyurethane"].
    ruling_plastics expects answers ["belt is made of plastics", "glove is made of plastics"].
    ruling_fibres expects answers ["bamboo is a word for the textile material viscose"].

query ruling_polymers is:
    the polymer of which good is which polymer.

query ruling_plastics is:
    which thing is made of plastics.

query ruling_fibres is:
    "bamboo" is a word for the textile material which material.

query polymers is:
    the polymer of which good is which polymer.

query plastics is:
    which thing is made of plastics.

query fibres is:
    "lycra" is a word for the textile material which material.

query goat fibres is:
    "mohair" is a word for the textile material which material.
